   967	  - `storeInv_on_block`:
   968	    - `closed`, `sub`: `hp`, and `TF` grows only with `T`.
   969	    - `admit`: a new block with `F ⪯ B` enters `TF`. F only moves to a descendant (`update_finality_F_mono`), so `F' ⪯ X` implies `F ⪯ X`, and `X ∈ TF` by the old invariant.
   970	    - `closedF`: take an admitted new `B ∉ st.T`. `F ∈ TF ⊆ T`, so `F ≠ B`. Then `F ⪯ B` gives `F ⪯ B.parent`, and `B.parent ∈ TF` by `admit` and `hp`. If `B ∈ st.T` already, `TF` does not change.
   971	    - `Fmem`: F moves only to `σ.F ∈ acceptViable ⊆ TF`.
   972	    - `hmax`: `frontier (insert B TF) = max (frontier TF) (h B)`. A block that is not admitted does not change `TF` or `h_max` (G04).
   973	    - `pair`: a new pair enters only if `F ⪯ σ.J` and it is lex-greater; otherwise the old pair stays the lex-max over the larger tree. When F advances to `σ.F ⪯ J`, the cached pair still has `F ⪯ J`. Every other pair with `new F ⪯ J'` also had `old F ⪯ J'`, because `old F ⪯ new F`. So the lex-max does not change. `hinj` makes the selected pair unique.
   974	    - `basis`, `bF`, `bW`: at an acceptance, `fBasis := {B, jCarrier, W}`: `(derive B).F = σ.F` (bF), `σ.F ⪯ W` (bW; the filter holds `σ.F` itself, since `σ.F ∈ TF`), and all three are in `TF`. Otherwise `fBasis` and `F` do not change, and `TF` grows. `derive` is a function of the block, so a saved carrier keeps its F.
