  1764	  - A `CHANGED` line means that a source changed after registration. Compare the pinned text of each entry that cites it. The registry gives a new id only when the statement or its hypotheses change; otherwise the async session updates the hash.
  1765	  - `KEY NOT IN §0.1`, `PATH NOT IN §0.1 ROW` or `HASH NOT IN §0.1 ROW` means that a `Src` does not match its registered source: fix the `Src`, or ask the async session.
