## 2026-09-26 — stronger sanity and accumulation witnesses

- Changed `Sanity.exampleRun` to take any integer delay `D`. It has one honest, awake proposer, a horizon of `max 1 (1 + D)`, and a tick at each public time through that horizon. `confirmedIncluded_claim_fails` now refutes the full inclusion claim for every `D`, including every valid nonnegative delay. `alwaysGenesis` permanently excludes objects; its state never processes them.
- Replaced the accumulation trace with four labels that act at times 0, 1, 2, and 3. At the first three labels, two honest seats vote for parent B and the faulty seat withholds a hidden-child X vote. `WithheldFaultyVote` records each faulty signature at its own act time; faulty signing is outside the engine's `Run.emits`. At label 3, Y is visible and both honest seats vote for Y. At time 4, the three X votes reach both honest nodes. Every label has two honest seats and one faulty seat.
- Proved `noFaultySeatDeliveryEarly` for every delivered object from a faulty seat. Proved honest vote emission, six spent B votes, two Y votes, three X votes, and loss of Y from an honest confirmed read between times 3 and 4. Pooled counting keeps all received seat votes across labels and uses no validator identity.
- Extended the run through time 5. `PartialSynchrony` includes delivery of the released faulty votes to both honest nodes before the relay deadline.
- Updated `docs/MAP.md`. `lake build --wfail` passed all 3317 jobs with the repository-local Lean wrapper. No network access, model or statement edits, `lake update`, or commit.

- Merged from the scratch clone into this repo by the Claude session (files AvailableChainWitnesses/, root file, lakefile lib, MAP section).

