     1	# FG composition registry (v2, 2026-09-28)
     2	
     3	_Owner: the async-resilience session (research). ethereum-f1 keeps this file
     4	consistent with FRAMEWORK-DESIGN.md §7._
     5	
     6	## 0. Registry policy (audit W08)
     7	
     8	- Each entry PINS its statement and its hypotheses. The pinned text is an
     9	  exact copy of the cited source lines. It does not change when the source
    10	  changes. Links inside pinned text are relative to `tsc/`.
    11	- Each entry names its module variant: `nj` (`SimplexFG.nj`, DC's NJ rule),
    12	  `fj` (`SimplexFG.fj`, the FJ root rule), or `both`. An AP-side entry names
    13	  the variant whose frame its premises use.
    14	- Each entry names its source file, section and line range, and the SHA-256
    15	  of that source file at registration (§0.1).
    16	- A change of statement or hypotheses gets a new id. The old id stays, with
    17	  the status WITHDRAWN. Ids with an unchanged statement stay.
    18	- The status is a dated line. A later status change adds a new dated line
    19	  below the old one. It does not change the pinned statement.
    20	- Status values: LEAN (a Lean certificate); PROVED (a paper proof from the
    21	  pinned hypotheses); PROVED* (a paper proof, conditional on the listed
    22	  unproved entries); SKETCH (a proof with an identified missing step); OPEN
    23	  (no proof and no refutation); REFUTED (a counterexample); RULE (true by
    24	  the honest code, not a theorem); def (a definition); WITHDRAWN (no
    25	  composite may cite the entry); SUPERSEDED (the entry stays as a pointer;
    26	  its pinned text does not change; a composite cites the named successor
    27	  ids, whose conjunction states the same fact).
    28	- Two edits of a hypotheses list keep the id, with a dated note: (a) the
    29	  replacement of a SUPERSEDED id by its successor ids; (b) a new reference
    30	  by id to a fact that the pinned text already uses (for example "F4" or
    31	  "finalized crossing"). Any other change of hypotheses gets a new id.
    32	- Pins to spec text resolve against `spec/archive/` by hash (rule added
    33	  2026-09-28): a pin to `spec/<name>.tex` with sha256 h refers to
    34	  `spec/archive/<name>-<first 8 hex digits of h>.tex`, whose sha256 is h.
    35	  The spec owner archives each registered spec version there before an
    36	  edit. The live `spec/` file can differ.
    37	- Research sources are archived by hash (rule added 2026-09-28): at
    38	  registration, the registry owner copies each pinned research source
    39	  that is not in Git to `<dir>/archive/<name>-<first 8 hex digits of
    40	  sha256>.<ext>` (for `tsc/`: `tsc/archive/`) and checks its hash. Pins
    41	  resolve against the archive copy with the registered hash, not against
    42	  the live file. A source in Git is recorded with its commit instead.
    43	- "FG-SA" in a status means a proof for the FG-SA client, that is, the
    44	  Simplex policy with honest non-equivocating signers. As a certificate
    45	  FAMILY over every policy σ, an AP-side entry still needs a proof that uses
    46	  only frame conditions and AP facts (FRAMEWORK-DESIGN.md §7.3, audit W02).
    47	  [async] An entry that states FG height progress is never a family entry;
    48	  it holds for the Simplex policy only.
    49	- AP-side ids (`ap.*`) state only AP SERVICE facts: repair, common fresh
    50	  sources, row service, block retention and source safety
    51	  (FRAMEWORK-DESIGN.md §7.3, audit W02). A height rise, an FG entry law or
    52	  a record permission is a `comp.*` or `fg.*` entry, derived after
    53	  specialization to the Simplex policy.
    54	
