   753	### `fg.frameCompat.v1` — "compatible with F" and "`F ⪯ J`" select the same pair
   754	
   755	- Variant `both`. Source: registry, 2026-09-28. No source file states this
   756	  lemma; the argument is below. Rule sources: dc lines 747–748, 762–767,
   757	  820, 824 and 838 (checkpoint heights); spec lines 361–365 and 494 (F
   758	  basis in every duty view); spec lines 736–750 (J guard and F basis).
   759	  Hashes as in `fg.frame.v2`.
   760	- Lean plan: DC-fj module, partial: (ii) only, F ⪯ J form (Lean
   761	  `fBasis_lexMax`, plan `befb5d5`). Changed 2026-09-28; the earlier line
   762	  was "none".
   763	- Hypotheses: R1 duty views (`env.r150` item 4; spec lines 483–495); the
   764	  F-basis rule of spec lines 742–750; the DC chain state (bp F5: one
   765	  height per block; the entry `T_h` is the block that entered h). It does
   766	  not use `a≤f`.
   767	- Statement (registry): let d be an honest duty with view V_d and current
   768	  accepted F = F_d. Let P1 be the greatest `(h_j, J.root)` justified pair
   769	  in V_d whose J is compatible with F (the `fg.frame.v1` rule). Let P2 be
   770	  the lex-greatest such pair with `F ⪯ J` (the `fg.frame.v2` rule). Then
   771	  P1 = P2. The same holds for the FJ frame: the wording "compatible with
   772	  F" of `env.r151` (r151 line 44) and the `F ⪯ σ[W].J` test of
   773	  `fj.frame.v1` select the same pair.
   774	- Proof (registry, 2026-09-28).
   775	  1. Checkpoint heights. A justified pair is `(h, T_h)` of a chain state
   776	     (dc line 824). `T_h` is the block that brought its chain into height
   777	     h (dc lines 747–748, 838), so `σ[T_h].h = h`. A finalized pair is a
   778	     former justified pair (dc line 820). The only exception is the
   779	     initial pair `(0, genesis)`, with `σ[genesis].h = 1` (dc lines
   780	     762–767). Thus each pair `(h,C)` has `h ≤ σ[C].h`, with equality when
   781	     C ≠ genesis. Heights do not decrease along a chain, and a non-genesis
   782	     entry T is the first block of its height on its chain. So every
   783	     strict ancestor of T has state height at most `σ[T].h − 1`.
   784	  2. Part (i): if `h_J ≥ h_F`, then "J is compatible with F" ⇔ `F ⪯ J`.
   785	     The direction ⇐ is immediate. For ⇒, suppose `J ≺ F` strictly. Then
   786	     F ≠ genesis, so `h_F = σ[F].h`, and step 1 gives
   787	     `h_J ≤ σ[J].h ≤ h_F − 1`. This contradicts `h_J ≥ h_F`.
   788	  3. Part (ii): V_d holds a pair with `F ⪯ J` and `h_J ≥ h_F`. If F is
   789	     genesis, every pair has `F ⪯ J` and `h_J ≥ 0 = h_F`. Otherwise
   790	     `update_finality` accepted F only with `σ.F ⪯ Σ.J` (spec line 742).
   791	     The F basis saved the J carrier W0, with `σ[W0].J = Σ.J` (spec lines
   792	     736–739, 749). R1 puts the F basis in every duty view (spec lines
   793	     363–365; HEAD view item 5, line 494; a full view holds every admitted
   794	     block). If `Σ.J = F` as blocks, then `h_J = h_F` (step 1, F ≠
   795	     genesis). If `F ≺ Σ.J`, then `h_J = σ[Σ.J].h ≥ σ[F].h = h_F`.
   796	  4. Each candidate of P2 is a candidate of P1, so P2 ≤ P1. Step 3 gives
   797	     `h(P2) ≥ h_F`, so `h(P1) ≥ h_F`. Step 2 gives `F ⪯ J` for P1, so P1
   798	     is a candidate of P2 and P1 ≤ P2. Thus P1 = P2. ∎
   799	- Status: 2026-09-28 — PROVED (registry argument; no Lean certificate).
