   125	/-! ## The pair rules and the record interface
   126	(PROTOCOL.md `def:antislashing`, `alg:pair-rules`)
   127	
   128	This module structures the two pair rules separately. They take plain fields and return a
   129	pair. `create_attestation` is the record's whole interface — "it takes the record
   130	and the vote information, produces the attestation, and updates the record before
   131	releasing it; it never reads the store" (PROTOCOL.md `def:antislashing`) — and
   132	`record_attestation` is the only writer.
   133	
   134	Two consequences, and both are semantic rather than cosmetic.
   135	
   136	* **`height_pair` sees its own attestation's lock.** It receives the finality
   137	  pair and overrides the lock at that height, so one attestation cannot form
   138	  E1 evidence (PROTOCOL.md `alg:pair-rules`).
   139	* **`target[h]` is written whenever a nonempty target is emitted at a fresh
   140	  height**, not only on the "no history" row. `record_attestation` folds the
   141	  emitted attestation, so the lock-repeat and target-repeat rows also write
